    "q-27598": {
      "dom_id": "step-q27598",
      "name": "Question 10",
      "problem": "Given that $\\operatorname{log}⁡(3x-2)=\\operatorname{log}⁡(8-2x),$ what is the value of $x?$",
      "worked_solution": "Since the logarithms on both sides of the equation have the same base, we can equate the arguments. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{log}⁡(3x-2) & =\\operatorname{log}⁡(8-2x) \\\\ 3x-2 & =8-2x \\\\ 5x & =10 \\\\ x & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's now check for extraneous solutions by substituting back into the original equation: \n\n- Substituting $x=2$ back into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{log}⁡(3(2)-2) & \\overset{?}{=}\\operatorname{log}⁡(8-2(2)) \\\\ \\operatorname{log}⁡(4) & =\\operatorname{log}⁡(4)\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $x=2$ is a valid solution.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-27598-a",
